From da4e440962a93952ac7090fa3d55046e01b9105e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-playground <rp@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:47:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Read crate metadata a page at a time on Emscripten hosts

There, mapping a file reads all of it into memory, so every crate a compilation
loads would have all of its metadata in memory: about 60 MiB for std alone, of
which compiling hello world decodes well under half. Instead, `.rmeta` files are
read through `MemDecoder::new_paged`, which loads 16 KiB pages as decoding reaches
them and keeps them for the crate's lifetime. With `-Zno-embed-metadata`, all
metadata is in `.rmeta` files; rlibs then hold only object code, for the linker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
